[31m+ # peer — spawn & talk to an ad-hoc colleague[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ > Route module — sibling-blind. Knows only this job; composition is the dispatch's job.[39m
[31m+ > Conventions cited as § C*n* live in `00-routing.md` § Shared conventions (pull lazily).[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ **Job**: talk to colleagues — stand up a NEW live session (claude / copilot / codex / pi) in a tmux pane, **or converse with peers that already exist**: identity/list/send/tail/state need no spawn. Nothing here delegates work products — this is the raw colleague seam.[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ **Preconditions**: follow § C1 for delivery-owner detection, native-extension ownership, exact-pane-only adoption and external register-first/no-pane-discovery rules. Spawn requires tmux. Tmux registration may place/reattach/export with `pij adopt "$TMUX_PANE" --harness <h> [--parent <id>] [--session-id <native-id>] [--export]`; carry an inherited parent (§ C1).[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ ## Verbs[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ **Identity — choose only the § C1 delivery owner's path**[39m
[31m+ ```bash[39m
[31m+ pij inbox register --json  # external pull FIRST: repairs exact ambient identity before whoami/list/state/tail[39m
[31m+ pij inbox --wait [ms]      # external: equivalent first-use registration, then receive[39m
[31m+ pij whoami [--json]        # external: only after registration; tmux control-plane: stable self[39m
[31m+ pij adopt "$TMUX_PANE" --harness <h> ${PIJ_PARENT_ID:+--parent "$PIJ_PARENT_ID"}  # tmux E-NOID only; exact non-empty current-process pane[39m
[31m+ ```[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ **Views**[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ ```bash[39m
[31m+ pij list [--here]        # known sessions (--here: this tmux server only)[39m
[31m+ pij state <id> [--json]  # liveness + working/idle for one peer[39m
[31m+ pij inbox --wait [ms]    # non-tmux receive path; first use auto-registers[39m
[31m+ pij tree [<id> | --global] [--activity <v>] [--liveness <v>] [--lifecycle <v>] [--all] [--json][39m
[31m+ ```[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ Bare `tree` selects the current Git repository across linked worktrees; `--global` selects the registry and `<id>` that subtree.[39m
[31m+ Dead/dissolved history is hidden unless `--all` or an explicit history filter exposes it.[39m
[31m+ Repeated values OR within one axis; activity, liveness, and lifecycle axes AND.[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ **Structure**[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ ```bash[39m
[31m+ pij link <child> --parent <parent> [--json][39m
[31m+ pij link <child> --root [--json][39m
[31m+ ```[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ `parentId` is structural: an id is an explicit parent, `--root` writes explicit root `null`, and absence keeps the legacy `spawnedBy` fallback.[39m
[31m+ `spawnedBy` remains close authorization; `link` changes no other descriptor fields. Unknown ids, self-parenting, and cycles fail before any write.[39m
[31m+ Use adopt `--parent <id>` at registration; spawn automatically records the caller as structural parent and close owner.[39m
[31m+ When giving work, the governor also passes `--role pm|worker` on `link`;[39m
[31m+ a seat never infers or self-declares its own role.[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ **Spawn**[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ ```bash[39m
[31m+ pij spawn --harness claude --model claude-sonnet-5 [--effort <level>] [--task "first task"] [--plan-id <id>] [--layout stack|right|below|window] [--branch][39m
[31m+ ```[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ Flags only: `pij spawn claude` is E-ARG; `--harness` is required. Effort is per-model[39m
[31m+ (`off|minimal|low|medium|high|xhigh|max`, warn-don't-block): discover with `pij models`, never assume.[39m
[31m+ `--plan-id` is opaque; it exports both plan env names, stamps the descriptor, and reports unresolved or non-segment ids without blocking spawn.[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ **Focus** — immutable native-session checkpoints, spawn's sibling:[39m
[31m+ `pij focus save <name>` requires a bound pi/claude caller; `pij focus list [--global]` is repo-filtered by default.[39m
[31m+ `pij focus launch <name>` forks a fresh tmux seat in **pending-canary**: golden recall must be verified (§ C2) before readiness.[39m
[31m+ pi launches from the main checkout, not a worktree; no copilot/codex adapters in v1.[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ File-change notices: `pij watch <path>` / `pij unwatch` — react to another seat's writes; mechanics in `docs/how/pij-peer-watch.md`.[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ **Body safety** (quoted text once EXECUTED `pij close` in a peer's repo): double-quoted[39m
[31m+ bodies expand backticks/`$(...)` in YOUR shell before pij runs. For code/backticks/untrusted[39m
[31m+ text, single-quote or use literal `pij send <id> --body-file <path>` (`-` = stdin).[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ - Model discovery is § C4; canary every spawned/provided peer before trust (§ C2), even after a non-blocking unknown-model warning.[39m
[31m+ - Returns id immediately: claude/copilot/codex bind asynchronously (boot → ready → bound); pi self-registers.[39m
[31m+ - `--task`: pi reads at boot via env; daemon-bound peers receive it after bind via inbox (FX001-2). `--branch` forks YOUR bound session, claude→claude only.[39m
[31m+ - Placement/default side stack: § C5. Seed § C10 in the first `--task` packet and require it for every subsequent send/reply.[39m
[31m+ - At each commit boundary, this seat and briefed peers apply § C11 (Commit attribution).[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ **Converse**[39m
[31m+[39m
[31m+ ```bash[39m
[31m+ pij send <id> "message text"                         # lands as an injected turn in one peer[39m
[31m+ pij send --to <id> --to <id> "message text"          # same text once to each peer, in flag order[39m
[31m+ pij send --to <id> --to <id> "message text" --wait   # wait for every successful recipient[39m
[31m+ pij send <id> --command compact                      # rs daemon control: compact | new | reload[39m
[31m+ pij compact-self                                   # daemon-resolved self; no literal slash fallback[39m
